# component: dialog
# decisions: A11Y-9, API-21, BRD-1, DOC-1, DOC-2, OVL-13, OVL-16, OVL-18, VOI-1
# hunks:
#   OVL-13: `DialogPortal` reads `useInternalThemeScope()` and wraps its children in a
#     `display: contents` element carrying that class, so a nested theme scope survives the jump
#     to `<body>`. The wrapper generates no box, so nothing about the backdrop's or the popup's
#     fixed positioning changes. `tooling/verify-portal-theme-scope.mjs` inventories this host.
#   A11Y-9: `DialogContent` mirrors Base UI's live `data-base-ui-inert` markers onto the native
#     `inert` property through `useModalInert`, so a focus guard that hands focus to `<body>`
#     cannot tab back into the background. The root now publishes its `modal` prop through a
#     context, which is exactly the shape upstream's own Drawer uses, because native inert would
#     also block the outside POINTER interaction that `modal={false}` and `"trap-focus"` keep.
#   BRD-1: `DialogContent` draws a real 1px `border border-border` instead of upstream's
#     `ring-1 ring-foreground/10` box-shadow outline (MK reversed BRD-1 to ours, 23-09-2026). A
#     border survives forced colours and matches `foundations/elevation`; nothing else moves.
#   OVL-16: `DialogContent` takes `size?: "sm" | "default" | "lg" | "xl"` (default `"default"`)
#     and reflects it as `data-size`, the axis `AlertDialogContent` already carries. `default` keeps
#     upstream's `sm:max-w-sm` unconditionally, so a consumer's `sm:max-w-*` className still merges
#     over it; `sm`, `lg` and `xl` step it to `max-w-xs`, `max-w-2xl` and `max-w-5xl` through
#     `data-[size=…]` (approved by MK 23-09-2026, a consumer gap).
#   API-21: `DialogBody` (`-mx-4 min-h-0 flex-1 overflow-y-auto px-4`, the focus-gutter idiom)
#     scrolls between the header and the footer band. A popup that holds one switches from
#     upstream's grid to a flex column capped at `max-h-[calc(100%-2rem)]` (upstream's own
#     `max-w-[calc(100%-2rem)]` inset, on the other axis) through `has-data-[slot=dialog-body]:`,
#     so a dialog without a body is untouched. `closeLabel` on `DialogContent` renames the corner
#     close control and on `DialogFooter` its opt-in close button.
#   VOI-1: both built-in close strings are the overridable `closeLabel` (default "Close").
#   OVL-18 (MK 2026-09-25): `DialogFooter` is as plain as the header — no `-mx-4 -mb-4`, no
#     `rounded-b-xl border-t bg-muted/50 p-4` band; it sits in the popup's own `p-4` with no divider.
#     The stack below `sm` and `sm:justify-end` stay upstream's. The `showCloseButton` close is
#     `variant="secondary"`, not `outline`: secondary actions in overlays are secondary.
#   cn: `import { cn } from "cn"` becomes `@vegastack/design` — our npm layer owns `cn` (DOC-2).
#   formatting: the repository formatter (prettier defaults: semicolons, trailing commas)
#               reflows the file, and `registry-stamp.mjs` writes the provenance header the
#               three-copy model needs (DOC-1); those hunks carry no decision of their own.
